    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! All frai-core tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**1. Governance module exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - These were previously only in the default export, causing the test import to fail with \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'join')\"\n\n**2. Toxicity metric signature** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n   - Updated `toxicityMetric` to accept `references` as a second parameter: `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)`\n   - Previously it only accepted `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, causing references to be incorrectly interpreted as banned terms\n   - This fixed the test expecting toxicity score of 1 but getting 0\n\n**Test Results:** \u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files  \n- All existing public exports remain functional and backward compatible",
